domain CompactV2ObservationStarvation:
  description |
    Record the observed replay monotony, distinguish its direct mechanism from
    broader production hypotheses, and select the bounded correction.

problem P1:
  |
    The successful Compact V2 replay satisfied its structural contract, but the
    ordinary scenario's second and third utterances both reported that the
    counterpart had not responded.

premise P2:
  |
    This replay is synthetic evidence. It can establish the harness inputs and
    model outputs that were recorded, but cannot by itself establish the cause
    of production battle monotony.

evidence E1:
  |
    The ordinary fixture authored three different event summaries: silence with
    a water ripple, a half-step and gaze movement, and a bell followed by the
    counterpart turning toward the character.

evidence E2:
  |
    The harness passed each authored summary only as prose on a wait TurnEvent,
    cloned the preceding perception frames while changing only their turn, and
    supplied no sensoryEvidence to advanceCharacterAgents.

evidence E3:
  |
    The retained run-state shows that ordinary turns two and three reached the
    psyche provider with only selfResult entries for the preceding utterance.
    counterpartResult and ambientChange were empty and the packet carried no
    source event IDs for the authored scene changes.

evidence E4:
  |
    On turns two and three the psyche responses repeated nearly the same
    observedImpact, nextApproach, continuityBasis, relationshipMove, and
    publicAim. The expression responses then differed only by adding まだ.

evidence E5:
  |
    The accepted observation contract derives TurnObservationPacket from a
    frozen CharacterPerceptionFrame and validated PerceptionEvidence. It
    intentionally does not mine free-form TurnEvent summaries for character
    cognition.

decision D1 based_on P1, P2, E1, E2, E3, E5:
  |
    For this replay, the root producing condition is a fixture integration
    mismatch: authored changes existed only as event-summary prose and were not
    represented as committed observer-safe sensory evidence. The observation
    projection therefore correctly omitted them. Production prevalence remains
    unknown.

decision D2 based_on P2, E3, E4:
  |
    The immediate monotony formed upstream of expression. With no new external
    result, psyche regenerated the same semantic move and expression realized
    that repeated brief. A separate contributing hypothesis is that an empty
    counterpartResult encouraged an unsupported non-response inference.

decision D3 based_on D1, D2, E5:
  |
    Keep the production observation and privacy contracts unchanged. Correct
    the replay fixture to create bounded PerceptionEvidence for each authored
    counterpart or ambient change, project it through projectObserverPerception,
    and pass the same evidence to advanceCharacterAgents. Never restore prose
    mining or inject a TurnObservationPacket directly.

decision D4 based_on P2, D3:
  |
    Add a network-zero preparation assertion that every ordinary psyche request
    after setup contains at least one fresh external item bound to the exact
    synthetic event ID. Record packet coverage in prepare-proof. Full real-model
    comparison remains a separate paid-call decision.
